{"title":"2017 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2c","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2017 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By finding a common denominator, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/f/23ff72be03eaa06690b47e6349cade434c034e6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/7/ea7648fb81a5ca94609c0b305f275abaf37d98b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{7}{21} &gt; \\frac{3}{21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"70\" height=\"38\" />. Similarly, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/1/8e1b92886d6361fc21ec08ba7a5cbd122a2de8cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{6} &lt; \\frac{3}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"52\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Fiona calculates her win ratio by dividing the number of games that she has won by the total number of games that she has played. At the start of a weekend, Fiona has played 30 games, has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> wins, and her win ratio is greater than 0.5. During the weekend, she plays five games and wins three of these games. At the end of the weekend, Fiona’s win ratio is less than 0.7. Determine all possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since she played <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> games at first and had <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> wins, her win ratio was initially <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/6/1362d7c5ab04067d1ad4535fd865464c4f891e93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{w}{30}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"34\" />. This was greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/2/192b4a258ee998961a99523fd0f0a029f9ea194a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.5$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" />, so we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/1/091e7fc9a35de62cbd45fefbd63c127ed61413f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{w}{30} &gt; 0.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"71\" height=\"34\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33ba4828d8edf7cffb79f1c98985c19268cc941.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w &gt; 0.5 \\times 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/6/51634d0bafb11725ff1375becb045bfc554953c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w &gt; 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Since she plays <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more games and wins <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> more, she must have played <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/9/649bed974692d04fd69003029b7a1242a91fd4eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30 + 5 = 35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" /> games in total and won <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/3/c435fc2058f6ac73a11d4201da630ae42188e7b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w + 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" /> games. Her win ratio was now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/4/50406116850d8a3a65b18cce3f0e52d1671d8a79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{w + 3}{35}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"51\" height=\"38\" />. This was less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/5/a3588bb395f693f5fd014687a9b680837fd2dc6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" />, so we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/e/89e11f104b40bd53886c22e9cfabe4c5e4ae7595.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{w + 3}{35} &lt; 0.7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"98\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/0/de02d2374393e6c0054832a6a20ebf8346cacaf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w + 3 &lt; 0.7 \\times 35 = 24.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"191\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/4/3b48e801b207d686b3e8431526d0b3153c6a0517.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w &lt; 24.5 - 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/e/fbea1f97254669e812cc51bfa1fa16ce1daddff5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w &lt; 21.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> must be an integer less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d111a5e00ee5ea6700bb629994dc629874c505b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Combining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/6/51634d0bafb11725ff1375becb045bfc554953c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w &gt; 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/b/83b2f20816c0659b36c21e0e9465e5fb7426b9c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w &lt; 22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" />, the possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/4/1e4274320dede35aa972ea2442ab81c08998b2cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{w = 16}, \\boxed{w = 17}, \\boxed{w = 18}, \\boxed{w = 19}, \\boxed{w = 20},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"375\" height=\"25\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/b/6ab973a51d7f068f4a28497dc84b22d742048d32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{w = 21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"69\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018003615\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.017 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.027 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 113/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 396/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5975/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.179      1 2017_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\n100.00%    7.179      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36950:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018003615 and revision id 285804. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}